1. Scope and definitions

"Licensed Material" means original software, tests, documentation, knowledge
explanations and protectable original selection or arrangement of structured
content made available under this licence by its rights holder. It includes
protectable modifications but excludes material identified in section 7.
"Licensor" means each rights holder granting rights in its own contribution.
"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising the permissions below.
"Your Organisation" means that entity and entities under common control with it.
Control means the power to direct management by ownership, voting or contract.
"Internal Use" means use for Your Organisation's own operations, including its
electricity business, compliance, audits, risk management and staff training.

2. Free permissions

Subject to this licence, each Licensor grants You a worldwide, non-exclusive,
royalty-free copyright licence to access, run, copy and modify its Licensed
Material for:
(a) Internal Use, including production deployment and internal integrations;
(b) personal learning, teaching, research, evaluation and non-commercial demos,
    including funded research that does not itself provide an offering restricted
    under section 4; and
(c) contributing improvements and sharing source copies or modifications without
    charging for access or copies, subject to sections 4 and 5.

You may keep internal modifications private. There is no requirement to publish
Your Organisation's modifications, private records, prompts or ordinary outputs.
These permissions last for the copyright term while You comply with this licence.
There is no automatic conversion to an open-source licence or automatic expiry
of the commercial restrictions.

3. Contractors, infrastructure and ordinary outputs

You may engage staff, advisers and contractors to deploy, host, configure,
integrate or maintain a private instance on Your Organisation's behalf and under
its control, solely for its Internal Use. They may charge for this work and generic
infrastructure. You must ensure they observe this licence and do not use this
permission to sell or operate a reusable third-party compliance product. Each
client must obtain its own applicable licence. General-purpose cloud or model
providers need no project commercial licence merely because You use their
infrastructure for a permitted purpose.

You may share ordinary results of permitted use with Your Organisation's customers,
auditors, regulators and advisers in the course of its own operations. For example,
a retailer may send a compliance explanation with an electricity bill. This does
not permit selling substantial Licensed Material as a content product or supplying
the services restricted by section 4. No rights are claimed in output merely
because the project produced it. Independently applicable source, copyright and
privacy rights still apply.

4. Commercial offerings requiring separate permission

Without a separate written commercial licence from the relevant rights holder(s),
You may not:
(a) sell, rent, sublicense for a fee or distribute for compensation the Licensed
    Material or a product substantially incorporating its protectable expression;
(b) supply a white-label or rebranded commercial version of the project to others;
(c) offer external users paid access to project functionality through a hosted
    service, SaaS, API, chatbot or other interface; or
(d) supply paid managed compliance-answering or monitoring services to third-party
    clients where project functionality is a substantial part of the service sold.

These restrictions also apply to payment bundled with another product, described
as a membership or service fee, or collected through an intermediary. Ordinary
Internal Use and the services expressly permitted by section 3 are not prohibited
merely because money changes hands. Charging for electricity, network services or
storage operations is not charging for this project. Independent consulting that
does not exercise restricted rights in Licensed Material is not prohibited.

A commercial licence may have separate terms and pricing. Requesting one, opening
an issue, receiving an automated reply or contributing does not grant it. Contact
the maintainer through the repository to arrange a private channel; do not post
confidential commercial details or personal records publicly.

